    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0140" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg20"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gummeré to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-07-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 33.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As I reported in my dispatch of July 3,
                    1905, according to the directions of the Department I announced the death of
                    Secretary Hay to Sid Hamed Torres, acting minister of foreign affairs, with the
                    request that he communicate the same to his government at Fez. I have now
                    further to report that I have received a letter from the said acting minister of
                    foreign affairs, a translation of which is inclosed, informing me that he had
                    received the reply to his said communication to the court, in which His Majesty
                    the Sultan commands him to express his deep regret and sorrow for the loss
                    sustained by our country in the death of Secretary Hay.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. R. Gummeré.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d47-a1.xml" xpointer="d47-a1"/>
            </div>
